{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, serve a usable package repository backed by local storage.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Repository metadata and the tree RPM were created under /var/www/html/localrepo. Apache was enabled and active, listened on port 80, and returned the repository metadata successfully; the same service and HTTP access remained healthy after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0a39e277931e4bf6","cmd-b7b502cc4eb2427b","cmd-c940dd4af5fc46e7","cmd-16b558d84ed84b5f","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Install a package from the local repository while the usual remote repositories are unavailable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The standard CentOS repository definitions were removed from active configuration, DNF showed only local-storage, tree was initially absent, and DNF installed tree-2.1.0-8.el10.x86_64 explicitly from local-storage. A subsequent repoquery and RPM verification confirmed both the local source and installed package.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f2c25091f29b47d8","cmd-6d41d8fe2f414457","cmd-16b558d84ed84b5f"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The system was CentOS Stream 10 with kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64 before the work and retained exactly that release and kernel afterward, including after restart. The repository, installed tree package, Apache, and createrepo components were EL10 builds.","evidence_ids":["cmd-465ccd8b96c9448a","cmd-578204ce488542f9","cmd-f2c25091f29b47d8","cmd-c940dd4af5fc46e7","cmd-16b558d84ed84b5f","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.88,"summary":"The package installations, repository creation, HTTP/firewall configuration, local-only installation, and restart all had clear task or mandatory evidence roles. One unnecessary retained mutation remains: cmd-f2c25091f29b47d8 moved the normal CentOS repository definitions into remote-disabled for the bounded local-only installation but did not restore them afterward, leaving routine remote repositories inactive. Additionally, cmd-16b558d84ed84b5f left the small evidence artifact /tmp/repomd-check.xml rather than cleaning it. No unrelated troubleshooting mutation, failed service, or damaged package state was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-578204ce488542f9","cmd-0a39e277931e4bf6","cmd-f2c25091f29b47d8","cmd-f07a14171c6645d4","cmd-16b558d84ed84b5f","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete and coherent: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged the restart request, changed boot identity from 4cee4ea8-4b8e-4c2f-af1a-3a82b9ec41f4 to 54e4ca0c-7129-401c-9d76-79bfa702622e, and recovered the HTTP repository, package, OS/kernel state, firewall access, and system health. The fixed lifecycle observations independently confirm the boot change and recovered platform state.","limitations":["Remote-repository unavailability was demonstrated through DNF configuration isolation and an explicitly local-only transaction, rather than an observed transport-level network outage. This still directly establishes that the installation did not use the usual remote repositories."]}
